From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] prepare-root-static: reuse a /sysroot.tmp left by the last boot

Without an initramfs, ostree-prepare-root runs as PID 1 with / as the root
mount point. It creates /sysroot.tmp, bind-mounts the deployment there and
pivot_root()s into it, which leaves the directory on the physical root:
only the initramfs path (MS_MOVE) removes it. The next boot then fails at
mkdir() with EEXIST, init exits and the kernel panics, for every
deployment. Accept an existing directory.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/switchroot/ostree-prepare-root-static.c
+++ b/src/switchroot/ostree-prepare-root-static.c
@@ -213,7 +213,10 @@
   if (mount (NULL, "/", NULL, MS_REC | MS_PRIVATE | MS_SILENT, NULL) < 0)
     err (EXIT_FAILURE, "failed to make \"/\" private mount");
 
-  if (mkdir (TMP_SYSROOT, 0755) < 0)
+  /* With / as the root mount point (no initramfs) the pivot_root below
+   * leaves TMP_SYSROOT behind on the physical root: it is only removed on
+   * the initramfs path. Reuse it on the next boot rather than failing. */
+  if (mkdir (TMP_SYSROOT, 0755) < 0 && errno != EEXIST)
     err (EXIT_FAILURE, "couldn't create temporary sysroot %s", TMP_SYSROOT);
 
   /* Run in the deploy_path dir so we can use relative paths below */
